{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#262","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#262","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#262\",\"parent_revision\":\"048b724188a81de46001dfe53c26502fb900731a\",\"root_revision\":\"2d022c299ab40815bffb2ad62fe7dfe93b4fe67a5d0ce0f49b6d33c315e79583\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWrap dasel CLI operations as MCP tools. Agents could query, transform, and convert structured data (JSON, YAML, TOML, XML, CSV) without shell piping. Tools: `query_data`, `transform_data`, `convert_format`, `install_dasel`.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaim: plugins/dasel/ v2.0.3 exists with install script and agents\\nTool: Read plugins/dasel/.claude-plugin/plugin.json; Glob plugins/dasel/**\\nResult: version 2.0.3 confirmed at line 3; plugins/dasel/scripts/install_dasel.py found; plugins/dasel/agents/ contains 3 agent files\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: plugins/frustration-analyzer/mcp/server.py and plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py use FastMCP 3.x + PEP 723\\nTool: Read plugins/frustration-analyzer/mcp/server.py lines 1-6; Read plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py lines 1-6\\nResult: Both files declare fastmcp>=3.0.0rc1,<4 in PEP 723 dependencies block with #!/usr/bin/env -S uv --quiet run --active --script shebang\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: dasel is a Go binary that reads from stdin and requires explicit -i/-o format flags (not a Python library)\\nTool: Read plugins/dasel/skills/dasel-reference/SKILL.md lines 8-36\\nResult: \\\"Single-binary CLI... Input is always read from stdin. Format must be specified explicitly with -i and/or -o.\\\" Source cited as internal/cli/query.go and internal/cli/run.go\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: agentskill-kaizen plugin.json uses inline mcpServers (single server, no separate .mcp.json)\\nTool: Read plugins/agentskill-kaizen/.claude-plugin/plugin.json\\nResult: mcpServers declared inline as {\\\"kaizen-analysis\\\": {\\\"command\\\": \\\"uv\\\", \\\"args\\\": [\\\"run\\\", \\\"--script\\\", \\\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/server.py\\\"]}} \u2014 no .mcp.json file referenced\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: dasel: Structured Data Query MCP\\nDate: 2026-04-19\\nGoal: Determine whether sufficient information exists to plan and implement a FastMCP 3.x server wrapping dasel CLI operations within the existing dasel plugin.\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent clear (4 named MCP tools, each operation defined) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description + Expected Behavior section\\n2. dasel plugin exists at expected location (plugins/dasel/) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Glob confirmed plugins/dasel/ v2.0.3 \u2014 plugins/dasel/.claude-plugin/plugin.json line 3\\n3. FastMCP 3.x PEP 723 pattern established in codebase | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read plugins/frustration-analyzer/mcp/server.py lines 1-5: fastmcp>=3.0.0rc1,<4; Read plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py lines 1-5: fastmcp>=3.0.0rc1,<4\\n4. Inline mcpServers plugin.json pattern verified | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read plugins/agentskill-kaizen/.claude-plugin/plugin.json: mcpServers inline with ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/server.py\\n5. dasel is subprocess interface (not Python library) | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read plugins/dasel/skills/dasel-reference/SKILL.md lines 8-36: single Go binary, reads stdin, -i/-o format flags required\\n6. Install script exists and handles cross-platform install | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Glob found plugins/dasel/scripts/install_dasel.py\\n7. Acceptance criteria defined and verifiable | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Prior grooming 2026-04-15 defined 7 numbered acceptance criteria in item body\\n8. Tool parameter schemas sufficient to implement | Snapshot: PARTIAL \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Expected Behavior section defines input/output contract for all 4 tools\\n9. No committed work blocked by this item | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Dependencies section + git log --grep dasel returned no output\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 5 (subprocess interface): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by Read of dasel-reference SKILL.md lines 8-36)\\n- Condition 7 (acceptance criteria): MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by prior grooming defining 7 verifiable criteria)\\n- Condition 8 (tool parameter schemas): PARTIAL \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by Expected Behavior section defining all 4 tool contracts)\\nAVAILABLE count: 9\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **dasel: structured data query mcp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: MCP backlog audit 2026-02-23\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-23\\n- **Research questions**: Evaluate whether wrapping the dasel binary (subprocess) or reimplementing core operations in Python is better for MCP transport.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested Location\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/dasel/mcp/server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Source |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent clear | AVAILABLE | Item description: wrap dasel CLI ops as 4 named MCP tools |\\n| dasel plugin exists | AVAILABLE | `plugins/dasel/` v2.0.3 with install script, agents, reference skills |\\n| MCP server pattern in codebase | AVAILABLE | `plugins/frustration-analyzer/mcp/server.py` and `plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py` using FastMCP 3.x + PEP 723 |\\n| FastMCP framework available | AVAILABLE | `/fastmcp-creator` skill; FastMCP used in 2+ existing plugins |\\n| Subprocess vs reimplementation | DERIVABLE | dasel is a Go binary reading stdin; Python reimplementation is not feasible |\\n| Tool parameter schemas | PARTIAL | Tool names given; input schemas and error contract undefined |\\n| Suggested location | AVAILABLE | `plugins/dasel/mcp/server.py` consistent with codebase pattern |\\n| Acceptance criteria | MISSING | No verifiable done-criteria in original item |\\n\\nMissing inputs are refinement-level and do not block planning.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 feature item. No existing broken behavior to reproduce. Acceptance criteria in \u00a7Acceptance Criteria serve as the verification baseline.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 Score: 5/10\\nRationale: Agents can use dasel today via Bash tool; no committed work is blocked. An MCP layer reduces friction for automated pipelines and eliminates shell string construction overhead, but the gap is a convenience improvement rather than a capability blocker.\\nEffort: Small \u2014 new FastMCP PEP 723 server (~150-200 lines), single plugin.json update (3 lines). Pattern established in two existing plugins. Estimated: half a day.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Nothing currently \u2014 no committed work depends on this MCP server\\n- Bottleneck: Agents querying large structured data files currently require explicit shell pipe commands via Bash tool; MCP tools make this directly callable from agent tool-use without shell construction\\n- Potential unlock: Automated data transformation pipelines and config mutation workflows that currently require shell orchestration\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Agents call `query_data`, `transform_data`, `convert_format` directly without constructing shell pipe commands\\n- Consistent calling convention across all 7 structured data formats (JSON, YAML, TOML, XML, CSV, HCL, INI)\\n- `install_dasel` tool enables self-healing: agent detects missing binary and installs before invoking other tools\\n- Reduces context consumption: targeted field extraction without loading full file content into context\\n- Agents building automation pipelines get a stable tool API rather than fragile shell string construction\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen the MCP server is running, `query_data` accepts a dasel selector and input data (as a string) plus input format, and returns the queried value. `transform_data` accepts a selector, a new value, and input data, applies the modification, and returns the full document. `convert_format` takes input in one format and returns it in another. `install_dasel` runs the existing install script and reports success or failure with a clear message. All tools return structured output \u2014 not raw shell output. If dasel is not installed, tools other than `install_dasel` return a clear error message pointing to `install_dasel`, not a subprocess traceback.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `plugins/dasel/mcp/server.py` \u2014 FastMCP 3.x PEP 723 script with four MCP tools\\n- `plugins/dasel/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` updated with inline `mcpServers` field (single server, inline is correct per `/plugin-creator:mcp-integration` for single-server plugins)\\n- Existing `plugins/dasel/scripts/install_dasel.py` invoked by the `install_dasel` tool \u2014 not duplicated in the MCP server\\n- No separate `.mcp.json` needed (single server uses the inline `plugin.json` pattern as in `agentskill-kaizen`)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run fastmcp list --command 'uv run --script plugins/dasel/mcp/server.py'` lists four tools: `query_data`, `transform_data`, `convert_format`, `install_dasel`\\n2. `query_data` called with input `'{\\\"foo\\\": \\\"bar\\\"}'`, format `json`, selector `foo` returns `bar`\\n3. `convert_format` with `'{\\\"key\\\": \\\"value\\\"}'` input format `json` output format `yaml` returns valid YAML\\n4. `install_dasel` when dasel binary is absent runs the install script and returns success or error (not a traceback)\\n5. Tools called when dasel is absent (except `install_dasel`) return a clear error message, not a subprocess crash\\n6. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/dasel` passes with no errors\\n7. `claude plugin validate plugins/dasel` passes\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /fastmcp-creator \u2014 FastMCP 3.x server creation reference |\\n| Skill | /fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-python-tests \u2014 pytest patterns for FastMCP tools |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:mcp-integration \u2014 MCP server config within plugins (inline vs .mcp.json decision) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/dasel/scripts/install_dasel.py` \u2014 existing cross-platform dasel installer (invoke from `install_dasel` tool) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/dasel/skills/dasel-reference/SKILL.md` \u2014 dasel v3 syntax reference including stdin/flag semantics |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/frustration-analyzer/mcp/server.py` \u2014 FastMCP 3.x + PEP 723 MCP server pattern to follow |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/agentskill-kaizen/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 inline `mcpServers` registration pattern |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/dasel/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 plugin file to extend with `mcpServers` field |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 dasel plugin exists; install script is functional\\n- Blocks: None \u2014 no committed work waits on this MCP server\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 FastMCP server wrapping a CLI binary with 4 tools. Install script exists; server is ~150-200 lines of PEP 723 Python. Pattern is established in two existing plugins. Plugin.json update is a 3-line addition. Estimated: half a day.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:4979c91ab0dadfd1c5c3e1939d85b1e3 -->\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nThe dasel plugin provides agents with structured data manipulation capability. Adding an MCP server layer directly extends this intent: the plugin already delivers skills for *knowing* how to use dasel; the MCP server enables agents to *call* dasel directly without constructing shell commands.\\n\\nThis follows the established codebase evolution pattern: agentskill-kaizen and frustration-analyzer both evolved from skill-only to skill+MCP-server when programmatic invocation became the primary use case. The proposed inline `mcpServers` plugin.json pattern and `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/server.py` path are byte-for-byte consistent with the agentskill-kaizen precedent.\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\nCitations: plugins/agentskill-kaizen/.claude-plugin/plugin.json (inline mcpServers precedent); plugins/dasel/.claude-plugin/plugin.json description (\\\"Query, transform, and convert structured data files... Provides reference syntax, exploration workflows, transformation patterns\\\"); 2 existing FastMCP server implementations in repo confirm this is an active, supported pattern\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: unbounded-design\\nRationale: Item was originally an open-ended feature request (\\\"Wrap dasel CLI operations as MCP tools\\\") with no tool schemas, no acceptance criteria, and no implementation decisions. The prior grooming session (2026-04-15) resolved all open questions and defined acceptance criteria. Classification reflects the original item type at intake \u2014 new capability requiring design decisions before implementation can begin.\\nAnalysis method: intake-classification (item started as feature with no boundaries)\\nScenario target: new MCP server within existing dasel plugin\\n\\n### Research Questions Resolved\\n\\n**Q: Subprocess (wrap dasel binary) vs reimplementing in Python?**\\n\\nResolved: Subprocess wrapping only. dasel is a Go binary with no Python port. The existing `plugins/dasel/scripts/install_dasel.py` handles cross-platform binary installation. The dasel-reference skill confirms dasel reads from stdin and requires explicit `-i`/`-o` format flags \u2014 this is a subprocess interface, not a library interface. The research question is closed.\\n\\nSource: `plugins/dasel/skills/dasel-reference/SKILL.md` lines 8-36 (dasel is a single Go binary reading from stdin); `plugins/dasel/scripts/install_dasel.py` (cross-platform install logic); codebase inspection 2026-04-15.\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| File | Change | Scope |\\n|------|--------|-------|\\n| `plugins/dasel/mcp/server.py` | New file \u2014 FastMCP 3.x PEP 723 script with 4 MCP tools | Create |\\n| `plugins/dasel/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` | Add inline `mcpServers` field (3-line addition following agentskill-kaizen pattern) | Modify |\\n| `plugins/dasel/scripts/install_dasel.py` | Invoked by `install_dasel` tool \u2014 no modification required | Read-only dependency |\\n| `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` | Version bump (auto-applied by pre-commit hook on commit) | Auto-bumped |\\n\\n**Blast radius**: Minimal \u2014 new file + 3-line plugin.json update. No existing agents, skills, or hooks in the dasel plugin are affected. No other plugins depend on the dasel plugin.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3743c3d0400cc68945fbae92bfb0eed87e05a747a5714553ca5654c80147059a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnMpPQ\"}"}